# elohim/sdk — source-of-record governance

## Portable app contract

`crates/elohim-sdk/src/lifecycle` and `storage-client-ts/src/app-lifecycle.ts` expose the portable
app interfaces. The wire types live together in `crates/elohim-views/src/app_lifecycle.rs`,
conform to the `schemas/v1/views/app-*` schemas and generate TypeScript. Missing implementations
refuse explicitly. Bounded demand leases are a lower-level Rust primitive, not a client scheduler.
Peer hosts retain app/session admission; doorway mounts browser ingress. A Che adapter must not
tunnel a loopback-only SDK route or spoof its caller. The live-session standard owns passing-state
channels; durable private observation reconciliation remains a different concern.

## Application lifecycle contract

The [root composition map](../../.epr-meta/composition.md#application-lifecycle--authoritative-homes-and-composition)
routes local work, collaboration, publication and serving. The existing
[working-version standard](../../genesis/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-04-working-version-sdk-standard-design.md)
owns their client lifecycle semantics: author schema vocabulary in `schemas/v1`,
domain choices in `domains/`, and reusable TypeScript behavior in `storage-client-ts`.
Keep the Rust SDK contract aligned. Browser persistence and offline resumption belong
in shared client support; UI frameworks bind it rather than implementing independent
queues, publication state machines or admission rules. Peer storage implements custody
and authorized sync; the notary decides publication authority.

The standard remains Draft: `AutomergeSync.load/save/sync` is not the full working-version
API. A sprint implementing a missing primitive must include its declared alone/offline
behavior and a consumer journey. Do not advertise proposed manifest fields as accepted
schema until the schema and its consumers implement them together.

This subtree is where vocabularies are BORN. The reach reconciliation (slices 1-3) and the
ontology keel (2026-07-23) are the case law: hand-typed vocabulary values outside a declared
source-of-record are the recurring defect class here.

Two conventions are authoritative but not gate-enforced in v1 because the closed predicate
vocabulary cannot soundly express path-aware generated-file detection or a required phrase
inside a JSON description:

- Files under a generated path are projections. Edit the schema, card, Rust view, or codegen
  source, rerun the relevant generator (`pnpm run schema:codegen:ts` / `cargo test
  export_bindings`), and commit source plus projection together.
- A new closed vocabulary states `Source of truth:` in its description, chooses its tier
  deliberately (`_dna` only through a deliberate DNA-lineage event), and considers an axis
  card in `registries/axes/` when it is an orthogonal coordinate. Exactly one generative
  source of record exists per vocabulary; every other appearance is generated or an explicit
  re-export.
